### Entry #067 — 2026-06-11

**User:**
> Point #13 next — Liveness detection improve (photo attack prevention)

**Claude:**
> Face Kiosk Point #13 implement kiya — Liveness detection actually wired up.
>
> **Bug found:** Previous "liveness check" collected `recentBoxes` but never used the variance — matching proceeded unconditionally. Box was collected but never read.
>
> **Changes in `src/pages/attendance/FaceKioskPage.tsx` (`startLiveLoop`):**
>
> - `livenessFrames` buffer: stores `{ x, y, size }` per frame (added `size = faceSize`)
> - `LIVENESS_FRAMES = 5` (was 3 — and was unused)
> - `MIN_MOTION_PX = 2.5` — required positional movement (Δx + Δy across frames)
> - `MIN_SIZE_CHANGE = 3` — required faceSize change across frames
> - `isLive()` function: `posVariance = (maxX-minX) + (maxY-minY)` + `sizeVariance = maxSize-minSize`; returns true if EITHER exceeds threshold
>
> **Loop flow change:**
> 1. Buffer < 5 frames → `"Scanning... (N/5)"` + continue collecting
> 2. Buffer full + `!isLive()` → `"Thoda hiliye... (photo detected?)"` + loop continues (no match)
> 3. Buffer full + `isLive()` → proceed to face matching as before
>
> Photo/screen attack: static face → zero variance → blocked at step 2.
> Real person: natural micro-movement (breathing, muscle) → variance threshold passed within ~3.5s.

**File Modified:** `src/pages/attendance/FaceKioskPage.tsx`

